00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:33.630
Ronja!

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.050
Ronja and Birk managed to reach the riverbank just before being gulped up by Greedy Falls,

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.010
and safely returned to the Bear's Cave.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.350
There they found Lovis, waiting for them.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.900
Ronja did not return to the castle with her.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:59.530
But now the forest leaves are aflame with the colors yellow and red.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.030
Fall has finally begun.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:11.620
Life Is Precious

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:11.620
Life Is Precious

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.420
Birk.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.090
I found some that aren't too damp.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.480
It's a rainy summer we're having.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.740
But, of course, it will get better.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:05.000
It's a windy summer we're having.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:10.550
But, of course, it will get better.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.250
It's a frosty summer we're having.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:49.090
My sister is not happy, is she?

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.720
It's about time for you to leave here...

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.980
...and warm yourself at some other fire, one that isn't mine.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:15.030
Another fire...

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:20.050
I won't be able to warm myself at the fire in Mattis' fort ever again,

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.870
for I am not his child.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:30.340
I'll come as soon as I get the fire going.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.990
My child... My child!

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.410
I have my child back!

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:52.340
<i>Am</i> I your child now, Mattis?

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:57.260
Am I really your child again?

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:02.600
Yes, you always have been,

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.060
and forever will be,

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:05.730
my Ronja!

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:12.940
My child, whom I have wept for night and day.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.650
Oh, how I've suffered!

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:29.920
Is it as Lovis said? Will you only come home if I ask you to?

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.590
Is that true?

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.830
Is it true, Ronja?

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:48.980
Will you come home with me now?

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.650
Come, Ronja.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.400
We're going now.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.170
But I haven't asked you properly yet, have I?

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.560
I ask you, Ronja, with all my heart...

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.560
Come home to me again.

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:46.240
Birk Borkason!

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.040
Come here!

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.790
I want to have a word with you.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:05.390
What do you want?

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:08.890
To give you a beating, honestly.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:14.900
But I'm not going to.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:20.190
Instead, I ask you with all my heart...

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:24.990
Come back to Mattis' fort with us now.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:25.970
Like this!

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:30.580
It's not because I like you.

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:33.460
Don't think that, whatever you do.

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:40.260
But my daughter does, I know that now,

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:45.260
and perhaps I can learn to as well.

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:50.720
I've had time to think about this and that these past months.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.240
Hey, Father.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:09.410
I need to talk to Birk alone.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:12.370
Why?

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:19.960
Oh well, I'll go and have a look at the scenery around my old Bear's Cave in the meantime.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.460
But!

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:25.260
Be quick!

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:29.390
We're going home now, after all!

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:46.950
We're going home now, huh?

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:52.160
What home?

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:58.290
Does he think I'm going to be
 the whipping boy for Mattis' robbers?

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.960
I'll never let that happen!

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:07.630
Whipping boy? How stupid are you?

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:12.220
Would you rather freeze to death in the Bear's Cave?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.640
Yes! I think so!

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:20.020
Life is something you have to treasure!

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:21.650
Don't you realize that?

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.650
If you stay in the Bear's Cave for the winter,

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:28.160
you'll be throwing your life away!

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:31.160
And mine as well!

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:34.370
Why do you say that?

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:39.170
How can I throw away your life?

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:40.500
Because!

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:46.920
If you stayed at the Bear's Cave, I would stay with you!

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.180
You numskull!

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:53.470
Whether you liked it, or not!

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:08.030
Do you realize what you're saying, Ronja?

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.120
I know!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:15.410
I'm saying that nothing can part us!

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:19.710
And you know that, too!

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:22.000
You numskull!

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.390
I don't want to throw away your life,

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.220
my sister.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.680
It's the last thing I want.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:42.060
I will go with you wherever you go.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:48.740
Yeah, even if I have to live among Mattis' robbers

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:51.780
until it chokes me.

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:03.790
I love you, Birk Borkason.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:19.520
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:19.520
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:43.040
Next spring, let's move back here again.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:48.840
Yeah, now that we'll be alive to see it.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:27.460
We'll be coming back!

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.920
Just keep safe!

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.260
You must!

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:50.860
Mattis.

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:59.410
I want to go home to Borka's keep first and see how thing are with Undis and Borka.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:08.210
But I give you my thanks for allowing me to come to Mattis' fort,

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:10.920
and meet Ronja whenever I like.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:16.380
Yes, yes. Well it won't be easy for me,

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:18.470
but come anyway!

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:27.940
You know what Skalle-Per has been saying?

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:30.050
The old fool is saying...

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:34.940
...that the best thing would be for Mattis' robbers and Borka's robbers to join forces,

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:41.830
before the Sheriff and his men catch us and hang us all.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:46.460
He's chock-full of crazy ideas,

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:48.290
that old idiot.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:52.710
It's a shame, isn't it?

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:55.260
That you have such a scoundrel of a father.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:17:00.680
If Borka were a better man, as crazy as that idea is,

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:03.850
he would at least be at least able to think it over.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:09.440
You may be a scoundrel too, though.

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:15.940
Now, let's go!

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:16.780
Yeah!

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.610
I'll be seeing you, robber's daughter.

00:17:20.610 --> 00:17:22.030
Everyday.

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.830
You know that, right? My sister.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.580
Yeah, everyday...

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.170
...Birk Borkason.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.040
I'm home!

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:19.880
Skalle-Per!

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:28.100
That was a welcome home greeting.

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:07.140
Mother!

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:11.520
Can you bring in the big washtub for me?

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:14.850
I've already got it ready.

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:17.020
The water has been heated too.

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.940
I figured as much.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:23.400
You're the kind of mother that thinks of everything.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:28.160
And have you ever seen a filthier child?

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:31.620
No, never in my life.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.080
I'm happy, truly!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:36.790
What?!

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:37.670
I'm so happy!

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.920
What's wrong with you? Bawling like that is just shameful!

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:43.470
What?!

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:47.180
You've been crying up until now as well!

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:48.050
Darn.

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:52.180
That wasn't crying, I was just wiping off some sweat.

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:55.230
Oh, your sweat spouts from your eyes?

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:56.310
That's rich!

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:57.020
What?!

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.100
You wanna fight?!

00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.180
That's just what I want!

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:03.400
Today's the day I beat you into pulp!

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.380
Birk!

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.510
Welcome back,

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:32.140
my son!

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:47.110
Birk!

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:16.520
Cheers!

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:30.590
Ronja!

00:22:31.420 --> 00:22:32.840
What's the matter?

00:22:32.840 --> 00:22:38.010
I just wanted to make sure that you're really there.

00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:45.020
Yes, of course I'm here.

00:22:45.020 --> 00:22:47.320
I see, good.

00:22:48.390 --> 00:22:53.340
Thus, everything had returned to the way it used to be.

00:22:53.840 --> 00:23:01.930
Ronja thought about Birk, and wondered how he was doing over at Borka's Keep.

00:23:02.530 --> 00:23:07.780
"I hope he's warm right down to his toes too."

00:23:08.260 --> 00:23:12.690
"I'll ask him tomorrow."

